 It reads a string `s` from stdin, then iterates over each character of `s` (by index) and checks if the current character matches the current expected character in `hi`.
 If it matches, it increments the counter. If the counter reaches the length of `hi` (5), it prints "YES" and returns.
 If the loop ends without matching all, it prints "NO".

 We need to translate this to PHP.

